1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:06,608
The brush clears a half-round mound of stone, topped by a small square railing and an umbrella.

2
00:00:06,608 --> 00:00:15,117
It is a stupa, a monument that holds a relic, a small piece of what remained after cremation. Why build a mound over a relic?

3
00:00:33,550 --> 00:00:42,498
How do we know? Buddhist texts record the councils. Archaeologists dug up stupas at Sanchi, Bharhut and Amaravati.

4
00:00:42,498 --> 00:00:46,648
Inscriptions on the railings name the donors who paid for them.

5
00:01:03,583 --> 00:01:08,792
After the death of the Buddha, the teachings needed to be kept. Four councils met.

6
00:01:08,792 --> 00:01:15,005
The first, at Rajagriha, was about 483 BCE, under Ajatashatru.

7
00:01:15,005 --> 00:01:19,939
Upali recited the rules of the order, and Ananda recited the teachings.

8
00:01:19,939 --> 00:01:26,106
The second, at Vaishali, was about a century later, and ended with a split in the order.

9
00:01:26,106 --> 00:01:35,340
The third was at Pataliputra, under Ashoka, led by Moggaliputta Tissa. After it, missions were sent out, including to Sri Lanka.

10
00:01:35,340 --> 00:01:42,372
The fourth was in Kashmir, under Kanishka. Here the Mahayana branch took shape, with texts in Sanskrit.

11
00:01:42,372 --> 00:01:48,669
The teachings were collected in three baskets, the Tripitaka: Vinaya, Sutta and Abhidhamma.

12
00:01:48,669 --> 00:01:54,877
Stupas spread, with carved gateways and railings at Sanchi, Bharhut and Amaravati.

13
00:01:54,877 --> 00:01:59,614
Monks also lived in viharas, and prayed in chaitya halls.

14
00:02:16,550 --> 00:02:24,128
Old name, new name. The older branch of Buddhism is often called Hinayana, the lesser vehicle.

15
00:02:24,128 --> 00:02:28,773
That is a name used by its critics, and many now consider it unfair.

16
00:02:28,773 --> 00:02:33,391
The name Theravada, the way of the elders, is preferred today.

17
00:02:50,317 --> 00:02:59,910
Carve this tip into memory. Rajagriha, Vaishali, Pataliputra. Kashmir: four councils. Four places, in order.

18
00:02:59,910 --> 00:03:03,596
Add a king to each, and you can write the whole answer.

19
00:03:20,517 --> 00:03:36,285
Dig Quiz. Pause and name it. Number one. Name this mound that holds a relic. The answer: a stupa. Number two.

20
00:03:36,285 --> 00:03:52,798
Which three baskets make the Buddhist canon? The answer: the Tripitaka. Number three. Where was the third council held?

21
00:03:52,798 --> 00:04:02,087
The answer: Pataliputra. Now one line for Mains. Trace the spread of Buddhism after the death of the Buddha.

22
00:04:23,017 --> 00:04:32,135
The stupa goes into its case. A small model stands for a great monument. Three facts to take away. A mound that holds a relic.

23
00:04:32,135 --> 00:04:40,992
Four councils, three baskets. Great stupas at Sanchi and Bharhut. Next gallery: Magadha Rises.

